Based on the excerpts provided, here's what I can tell you about Flood cover:

**Cover provided:**
Flood is listed as an Insured Event (Insured Event 12) under the RAA Contents PDS. The policy provides cover for loss or damage to the "Insured Property" as a result of Flood [RAA Contents PDS, page 50]. The excerpts do not specify separately whether this applies to "Home" (building) or "Contents" categories, but the term "Insured Property" suggests it can apply to whichever category (Home and/or Contents) is shown on your Certificate of Insurance.

**Key exclusions that apply to Flood cover:**
This cover does **not** apply to loss or damage:
- to any part of the Home that is not fully built;
- to tennis courts;
- to a wharf, jetty, pontoon or sea wall;
- to water in a tank, swimming pool or spa, including cleaning costs for mud/debris in these;
- to swimming pools or spas and their covers/liners, except permanently attached hard lid style pool covers;
- to paint, unless there is structural damage caused by Flood to other parts of the Home;
- caused by underground (hydrostatic) water;
- to a glasshouse or greenhouse;
